{"name": "Roguish Archetype: Corsair", "type": "archetype", "img": "icons/sundries/flags/banner-flag-pirate-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Subclass for the @Compendium[undertaking.classes.I9VDL0C1Q1G7YHVO]{Rogue} class.</p><p>When it comes to thieves, few professions can boast the fame and notoriety that surrounds the Corsairs of the high seas. The tales of their voyages are filled to the brim with daring acts of piracy and enviable riches, along with a hearty serving of betrayal. Even with such dangers, the life of the Corsair calls to any Rogue with a spark of wanderlust and adventure in their soul. To truly succeed as a Corsair, one needs not just a capable crew but also the charm and daring to lead them, else the ever-present whispers of avarice may begin to stir mutiny in their hearts of those you rely on most.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "identifier": "rogue-corsair", "classIdentifier": "rogue", "classDetails": "<h3>Roguish Archetype: Corsair</h3><p><i>Unlock:</i> Have the Rogue Starter Abilities.</p><hr/><p>&#x1F193; Given Abilities: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.HLOE5LYM9Y1M9U58]{Dead Men Tell No Tales}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.EDSSCUMXYUHNCQ9F]{Panache}</p><hr/><h3>Corsair Abilities</h3><p>When taking a level in Corsair, you may choose from the following abilities: </p><hr/><p>Options: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.W6WA5QK7MVTV83IS]{Boarding Party}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.OVP7QML1V8RHMWEZ]{Rigged Fight}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.LYCMR7TCA8JCT44F]{Rakish Charm}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.EW5EDFT4VENBU9QJ]{Contingency Plan}</p>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "F4I7KZA6NOAD3J2I", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Martial Archetype: Defender", "type": "archetype", "img": "icons/equipment/shield/heater-steel-sword-yellow-black.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Subclass for the @Compendium[undertaking.classes.V29B5QR22SYWVP8K]{Fighter} class.</p><p>A knight in shining armor plants his tower shield and sturdies his stance as the beast lunges towards the party gathered behind him. A minotaur, buckler in hand, places herself in front of her bard companion as the atmosphere in the tavern turns violent. While every Fighter's goal is to be the one still standing when the battle is over, Fighters who follow the path of the Defender take a more hands-on approach to making sure their allies can be counted among the standing as well. To this end, their training goes beyond just mastering their weapon techniques to include many specialized defensive techniques.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "identifier": "fighter-defender", "classIdentifier": "fighter", "classDetails": "<h3>Martial Archetype: Defender</h3><p><i>Unlock:</i> Have the Fighter Starter Abilities.</p><hr/><p>&#x1F193; Given Abilities: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.5A7HOEBVANPTZD28]{Fighting Stance: Defender}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.IJ4DSNSC69UF86HZ]{Vigilant}</p><hr/><h3>Defender Abilities</h3><p>When taking a level in Defender, you may choose from the following abilities: </p><hr/><p>Options: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.UN7U2EJY5GRE4EB6]{The Best Defense}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.G5GV21SNLQ4Q8K8C]{Retribution}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.HS30FINEX9HB4RZE]{Heads Up}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.N5DFPGT4NAZQ3RM9]{Heroic Adrenaline}</p>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "4J3UKB8YI7P8IJEZ", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Divine Dominion: Dragon Dominion", "type": "archetype", "img": "icons/creatures/reptiles/dragon-horned-blue.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Subclass for the @Compendium[undertaking.classes.MV42LV7JCIELKCRM]{Cleric} class.</p><p>Clerics of the Dragon Dominion are drawn to the awe and power exuded by dragons and draconic deities. For some, dragons are like unto a class of divine beings of their own - demigods of flesh, blood, and flame to be showered with all the appropriate praise and offerings. To others, they represent an ideal to strive towards - a powerful body infused with magical power, complete with timeless wisdom. Whatever the motivation, it's common for Dragon Clerics to try to emulate their idols in some way, be it in mannerism, appearance, or both.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Those who have yet to meet a Cleric of the Dragon Dominion might expect them all to be crazed cultists willing to cast aside their morality for a taste of destructive power. While the sort power and riches boasted by dragons is always bound to draw sycophants, know that the path of the Dragon Dominion Cleric is no small undertaking. Learning to wield the raw power of the elements and live up to the ancient legacy of the dragons is bound to change a Cleric. For all those who may come to believe that might makes right, there are just as many who take after dragonkind's more wisened or benevolent examples.</p><h4>Dragon Dominion Proficiencies</h4><p>If this Divine Dominion is taken during character creation, you gain the following additional proficiencies:</p><p><strong>Weapons:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>(a) two simple weapons, or (b) a martial weapon</li><li>One crossbow (light, hand, heavy, or repeating)</li></ul><p><strong>Save Checks:</strong> Constitution</p><p><strong>Skills and Trades:</strong> Choose one of the following skills or trades to be proficient in: Intimidation, Athletics, Instinct, Culture, Artisan (Jeweler) Trade.<br /><br /></p><h4>Dragon Dominion Equipment</h4><p>If this Divine Dominion is taken during character creation, you gain the following additional equipment:</p><ul><li>(a) a simple weapon, (b) a pike (if proficient), or (c) a lance (if proficient).</li><li>(a) a simple ranged weapon and 20 ammunition, or (b) a repeating crossbow and 20 bolts (if proficient).</li></ul><p>Alternate Rule: Instead of taking any equipment from this section, instead take 2d4 x 10gp and spend it on items from the equipment section.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Anything bought this way cannot be magical, with the exception of magical foci, and no equipment can be modified mechanically from their base state.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "identifier": "cleric-dragon", "classIdentifier": "cleric", "classDetails": "<h3>Divine Dominion: Dragon Dominion</h3><hr/><h3>Dragon Dominion Starter Abilities</h3><p>As your first level in this dominion, you gain all of the following abilities: </p><hr/><p>Starter Abilities: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.UROYUWYQ5D1XOMRC]{Elemental Affinity}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.PF2GG3QRNRTNOXYS]{Dominion Spells}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.BP376DKTF70JKEHV]{Fearsome Presence}</p><hr/><h3>Dragon Dominion Abilities</h3><p>When taking a level in Dragon Dominion after your first, you may choose from the following abilities: </p><hr/><p>Options: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.B1NJPCKFFLL7PFVJ]{Eikon: Dragon}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.JKVO726WWVKAVE2W]{Hoarded Blessings}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.D1GJLP59RK0A613P]{Covetous Defiance}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.4RLLUUNYF7O4NQJ6]{Purloined Essence}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.DF3V1QA5MH23X8LZ]{Miracles of Draconic Transubstantiation}</p>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "DRGNL8BGELQQ9QAY", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
{"name": "Divine Dominion: Natural Dominion", "type": "archetype", "img": "icons/environment/wilderness/tree-spruce-green.webp", "system": {"description": {"value": "<p>Subclass for the @Compendium[undertaking.classes.MV42LV7JCIELKCRM]{Cleric} class.</p><p>Clerics of the Natural Dominion possess a reverence for the natural world and its many facets. They embrace the cycles of the world, from the seasons to the tides, and respect the role that each of its inhabitants plays, from the smallest insect to the largest whale. Indeed it is this very belief - that nature holds a place for all of us - that forms the bedrock for many a Natural Cleric.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;To those who have not met a Cleric of the Natural Dominion, one might assume they are bound to resemble unwashed, antisocial hedge-wizards. While this may be the case for some, don't forget that the races of the world too were birthed by and are part of nature. For many Natural Clerics, their calling is to mediate between the realms of civilization and the primeval, creating a greater harmony that safeguards both.</p><h4>Natural Dominion Proficiencies</h4><p>If this Divine Dominion is taken during character creation, you gain the following additional proficiencies:</p><p><strong>Weapons:</strong>&nbsp;</p><ul><li>(a) two simple weapons, or (b) a martial weapon</li><li>(a) Blowgun, (b) Longbow, (c) Shortbow, or (d) Slingshot</li></ul><p><strong>Save Checks:</strong> Constitution</p><p><strong>Skills:</strong> Choose one of the following skills to be proficient in: Instinct, Intimidation, Nature, Stealth, Theology.<br /><br /></p><h4>Natural Dominion Equipment</h4><p>If this Divine Dominion is taken during character creation, you gain the following additional equipment:</p><ul><li>(a) a simple weapon, (b) a battleaxe (if proficient), or (c) a trident (if proficient).</li><li>(a) a simple ranged weapon and 20 ammunition, or (b) a longbow and 20 arrows (if proficient) or (c) a blowgun and 20 ammunition (if proficient).</li><li>You can choose to keep the holy focus granted by core Cleric or replace it with a druidic focus.</li></ul><p>Alternate Rule: Instead of taking any equipment from this section, instead take 2d4 x 10gp and spend it on items from the equipment section.<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;Anything bought this way cannot be magical, with the exception of magical foci, and no equipment can be modified mechanically from their base state.</p>", "chat": "", "unidentified": ""}, "source": "Core Rules", "identifier": "cleric-natural", "classIdentifier": "cleric", "classDetails": "<h3>Divine Dominion: Natural Dominion</h3><hr/><h3>Natural Dominion Starter Abilities</h3><p>As your first level in this dominion, you gain all of the following abilities: </p><hr/><p>Starter Abilities: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.5APSGJ7C1CI9DA0F]{Dominion Spells}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.JWVFZMLVKQEYJGVO]{Wisdom of the Wilderness}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.7YFK8JVWZMT9FTKS]{Nature Provides}</p><hr/><h3>Natural Dominion Abilities</h3><p>When taking a level in Natural Dominion after your first, you may choose from the following abilities: </p><hr/><p>Options: @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.TNH2VR3UUITQYIWG]{Eikon: Nature}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.P97169W6CB1L94C4]{Fruitful Faith}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.ES1J6R9RFQJ33HVU]{Seasons of Faith}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.J1I3ZN58X2VSQ2YJ]{Squeak Easy}, @Compendium[undertaking-homebrew.abilities.1YD5VVREY3QRIR5L]{Miracle: Spirit Animal}</p>"}, "effects": [], "folder": null, "sort": 0, "ownership": {"default": 0}, "flags": {}, "_id": "C17L6G6K0LW4KTK4", "_stats": {"systemId": "undertaking", "systemVersion": "1.0.0", "coreVersion": "11.304"}}
